Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from RFC 6386
(VP8 Data Format and Decoding Guide), its prose and tables. They are not
translations of, and do not derive from, any other VP8 implementation's
source: not libvpx, not FFmpeg's libavcodec, and not the reference decoder
whose source RFC 6386 attaches (its section 20), which was not read. The
probability, quantiser and filter tables are reproduced from RFC 6386;
docs/PROVENANCE.md records the sections they come from and how each place
the RFC leaves open was settled.

The decoder is verified against the VP8 comprehensive test vectors
(vp80-00-comprehensive-001 to -018) and the MD5s of their decoded frames,
from the WebM project's public test data; tests/data/README.md gives their
source. They are bitstream data only; no implementation was run to make or
check anything in this crate.

